# Construction Scene Intelligence & Spatial Understanding

A multimodal computer vision system for construction-site scene understanding.

This project analyzes construction-site images and videos using object detection, segmentation, depth estimation, tracking, and vision-language reasoning.

## Planned Features

- Object detection using YOLOv8
- Promptable segmentation using SAM2
- Relative depth estimation using MiDaS/DPT
- Object-level spatial summaries
- Vision-language scene reasoning using Molmo/LLaVA-style models
- Structured scene reports
- Streamlit demo interface

## Project Roadmap

### Phase 1: Object Detection
- Run YOLOv8 on construction-site images
- Save bounding boxes as JSON/CSV
- Generate visualizations

### Phase 2: Segmentation
- Use detected boxes as prompts for SAM2
- Save object masks
- Overlay masks on images

### Phase 3: Spatial Understanding
- Estimate relative depth
- Combine boxes, masks, and depth into object-level scene summaries

### Phase 4: Vision-Language Reasoning
- Generate natural-language scene descriptions
- Answer questions about image content
- Produce structured reports


